image datasets. The proposed approach should address challenges related to low image contrast, thin and
irregular fracture boundaries, severe class imbalance, limited annotated data, boundary inaccuracies, and
computational complexity. The proposed improvements should be supported by mathematical models,
theoretical proofs, or experimental implementations and validated through comparative analysis and
ablation studies against existing segmentation models. The effectiveness of the proposed framework
should be demonstrated in terms of segmentation accuracy (Dice coefficient, IoU, precision, recall,
pixel accuracy, and Hausdorff distance), class-wise (particularly fracture) performance, model complex-
